      "output": {
        "message": "That adds an extra layer to manage, but you don't have to navigate all of them at once. Here are a few ways to handle that right now: 1. **Mute the group chat.** Put the shared thread on silent for a few days. You don’t need to announce you’re doing it, but seeing casual banter or notifications right now will just add unnecessary noise.\n2. **Lean on one person individually, if there's someone you trust.** If there is a particular friend in that group who can hold space without gossiping or taking it straight to your ex, reach out to them one-on-one. You don't have to broadcast the news to everyone at once.\n3. **Have a simple one-liner ready.** If someone from the group asks what's going on, you don't owe them a breakdown. A brief: *\"We broke up yesterday. I'm taking a little space right now to process things, but I'll catch up with everyone soon\"* is enough to protect your peace without creating drama. Have you already told anyone in the group, or has it stayed between the two of you so far?",
